# Vercel Web Analytics Integration

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js App Router project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` package using npm
- Updated package.json and package-lock.json with the new dependency

### 2. Analytics Component Integration
**Modified: `app/layout.tsx`**
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component inside the `<body>` tag, after the WalletProvider children
- Placement ensures analytics tracking is available across all pages while preserving the existing component structure

## Implementation Details
The project uses Next.js App Router (app directory), so the Analytics component was added to the root layout file. This ensures that analytics tracking is enabled across all routes in the application.

The component was placed after the main content (`{children}`) but inside the `<body>` tag, following Vercel's best practices for Web Analytics integration.

## Verification Steps Completed
✅ Package installed successfully (978 packages added)
✅ Build completed successfully - no errors
✅ Linting passed with no warnings or errors
✅ All changes staged with git (app/layout.tsx, package.json, package-lock.json)

## Technical Notes
- The project structure preserved: WalletProvider wrapping, font configurations, and metadata unchanged
- Analytics will automatically track page views and web vitals when deployed to Vercel
- No additional configuration required - the component works out of the box
- The implementation follows the official Vercel Analytics documentation for App Router projects
